WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.909
Read the coefficients
This quadratic equation has complex coefficients. Begin by calculating delta.
There is no need to classify a general complex discriminant as positive or
negative.

2
00:00:13.909 --> 00:00:26.909
Form the discriminant
The leading coefficient is one. To find delta, square two plus i, then
subtract four times the constant term, one plus i.

3
00:00:26.909 --> 00:00:39.909
Simplify
Expand the square using i squared equal to minus one. The imaginary terms
cancel on subtraction, leaving delta equal to minus one.

4
00:00:39.909 --> 00:00:56.545
Choose a square root
We need a number whose square is delta. The number i works because i squared
is minus one. Use i in the formula with both the plus and minus signs.

5
00:00:56.545 --> 00:01:12.273
Calculate the solutions
With the minus sign, the imaginary parts cancel and the result is one. With
the plus sign, two plus two i divided by two gives one plus i.

6
00:01:12.273 --> 00:01:27.545
Verify
Finally, check the sum and product of the roots. The sum is two plus i, and
the product is one plus i, matching the original equation's coefficients.
